  "problem": "Express $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{330}^{\u2218})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{330}^{\u2218})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v={330}^{\u2218}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x-{330}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{330}^{\u2218}+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{330}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
